  "body": "Recently [a new WPT was upstreamed](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/32709) from [chromium](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3440087), that shows that fonts are special-cased in `<link rel=preload>`, where their `crossorigin` attribute is ignored and always uses `anonymous` as that's the default way fonts are preloaded.\r\n\r\nThis seems to be the current behavior in Firefox and Chrome but is not specified (the current spec doesn't special-case fonts).\r\nIs this the desired behavior? It's possible that we would want to allow loading fonts with credentials in the future as per [this request](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/3194) and the [URL modifiers proposal](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1603) in CSS, which would make the current behavior of ignoring `crossorigin` counterintuitive?",
